{"abstract":"We propose Neuro-Symbolic Hierarchical Rule Induction, an efficient interpretable neuro-symbolic model, to solve Inductive Logic Programming (ILP) problems. In this model, which is built from a pre-defined set of meta-rules organized in a hierarchical structure, first-order rules are invented by learning embeddings to match facts and body predicates of a meta-rule. To instantiate, we specifically design an expressive set of generic meta-rules, and demonstrate they generate a consequent fragment of Horn clauses. As a differentiable model, HRI can be trained both via supervised learning and reinforcement learning. To converge to interpretable rules, we inject a controlled noise to avoid local optima and employ an interpretability-regularization term. We empirically validate our model on various tasks (ILP, visual genome, reinforcement learning) against relevant state-of-the-art methods, including traditional ILP methods and neuro-symbolic models.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Glanois, Claire","Jiang, Zhaohui","Feng, Xuening","Weng, Paul","Zimmer, Matthieu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382644"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd.","Shanghai Jiao Tong University"],"keyword":["Hierarchical Rule Induction","Inductive Logic Programming","Interpretability Regularization","Neuro Symmetric Modeling","Reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neuro symbolic hierarchical rule induction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101336608/2112.13418.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382644","identifier":[{"id":"85144257316","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5c351e3b-b546-48d1-85ab-dff6e6088b68"],"keyword":["Hierarchical Rule Induction","Inductive Logic Programming","Interpretability-Regularization","Neuro-Symmetric Modeling","Reinforcement Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-CDF9B9635E5EF941679B0CA06C066546"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2112.13418","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101336608/2112.13418.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"huawei technologies co ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huawei Technologies Co., Ltd.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhaohui","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Zhaohui","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xuening","key":"fengpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Xuening","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"wengpau","last":"Weng","name":"Weng, Paul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthieu","key":"zimmerpau","last":"Zimmer","name":"Zimmer, Matthieu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["26403498"],"issue":"39","journal":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","pages":"7583-7615","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","volume":"162"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144257316"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5c351e3b-b546-48d1-85ab-dff6e6088b68"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neuro-symbolic hierarchical rule induction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382644","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In contrast to deep reinforcement learning agents, biological neural networks are grown through a self-organized developmental process. Here we propose a new hypernetwork approach to grow artificial neural networks based on neural cellular automata (NCA). Inspired by self-organising systems and information-theoretic approaches to developmental biology, we show that our HyperNCA method can grow neural networks capable of solving common reinforcement learning tasks. Finally, we explore how the same approach can be used to build developmental metamorphosis networks capable of transforming their weights to solve variations of the initial RL task.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Najarro, Elias","Sudhakaran, Shyam","Glanois, Claire","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381397"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biological neural networks","HyperNCA","Neural Cellular Automata","metamorphosis networks","self organized developmental process"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hypernca growing developmental networks with neural cellular automata","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.11674","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381397","ids":["itu-099e48ae-434e-48d0-ad58-ec423e84d5d1"],"keyword":["HyperNCA","biological neural networks","metamorphosis networks","neural cellular automata","self-organized developmental process"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CD59130E627483E1D80EA92262A79812"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92842983/10.4324_9780429355950_14_chapterpdf.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.11674","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shyam","key":"sudhakaranpau","last":"Sudhakaran","locid":"b4a6e67f-0caa-4faf-a136-bf77496f3659","name":"Sudhakaran, Shyam","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19765541"],"issn_org":["23318422"],"journal":"arXiv","publisher":"arXiv","status":"p","title":"arXiv"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-099e48ae-434e-48d0-ad58-ec423e84d5d1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"HyperNCA: Growing Developmental Networks with Neural Cellular Automata","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381397","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We consider the problem of learning fair policies in (deep) cooperative multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL). We formalize it in a principled way as the problem of optimizing a welfare function that explicitly encodes two important aspects of fairness: efficiency and equity. We provide a theoretical analysis of the convergence of policy gradient for this problem. As a solution method, we propose a novel neural network architecture, which is composed of two sub-networks specifically designed for taking into account these two aspects of fairness. In experiments, we demonstrate the importance of the two sub-networks for fair optimization. Our overall approach is general as it can accommodate any (sub)differentiable welfare function. Therefore, it is compatible with various notions of fairness that have been proposed in the literature (e.g., lexicographic maximin, generalized Gini social welfare function, proportional fairness). Our method is generic and can be implemented in various MARL settings: centralized training and decentralized execution, or fully decentralized. Finally, we experimentally validate our approach in various domains and show that it can perform much better than previous methods, both in terms of efficiency and equity.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Glanois, Claire","Zimmer, Matthieu","Siddique, Umer","Weng, Paul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382936"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai Jiao Tong University"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Decentralized algorithm","Fairness","Multi Agents Systems","Reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"learning fair policies in decentralized cooperative multi agent reinforcement learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2012.09421","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382936","identifier":[{"id":"85149945597","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6ffa67f0-032b-4178-b30c-978c419d706b"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Decentralized Algorithm","Fairness","Multi Agents Systems","Reinforcement learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3B9A37BFF2DB7B228758EFFB92DEBCE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2012.09421","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"http://proceedings.mlr.press/v139/zimmer21a/zimmer21a.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthieu","key":"zimmerpau","last":"Zimmer","name":"Zimmer, Matthieu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Umer","key":"siddiquepau","last":"Siddique","name":"Siddique, Umer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"wengpau","last":"Weng","name":"Weng, Paul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2012.09421","issn":["26403498"],"journal":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","volume":"139"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6ffa67f0-032b-4178-b30c-978c419d706b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Learning Fair Policies in Decentralized Cooperative Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382936","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces EvoCraft, a framework for Minecraft designed to study open-ended algorithms. We introduce an API that provides an open-source Python interface for communicating with Minecraft to place and track blocks. In contrast to previous work in Minecraft that focused on learning to play the game, the grand challenge we pose here is to automatically search for increasingly complex artifacts in an open-ended fashion. Compared to other environments used to study open-endedness, Minecraft allows the construction of almost any kind of structure, including actuated machines with circuits and mechanical components. We present initial baseline results in evolving simple Minecraft creations through both interactive and automated evolution. While evolution succeeds when tasked to grow a structure towards a specific target, it is unable to find a solution when rewarded for creating a simple machine that moves. Thus, EvoCraft offers a challenging new environment for automated search methods (such as evolution) to find complex artifacts that we hope will spur the development of more open-ended algorithms. A Python implementation of the EvoCraft framework is available at: github.com/real-itu/Evocraft-py.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Berg Palm, Rasmus","Najarro, Elias","Glanois, Claire","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382906"],"event":{"acronym":"EvoApplications","title":"European Conference on the Applications of Evolutionary Computation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary computation","MIECRAFT","Open ended evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evocraft a new challenge for open endedness","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421848/2012.04751.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382906","ids":["itu-6e406c79-2b12-4d2d-a7ab-a2aa0aedef80"],"keyword":["Evolutionary computation","MIECRAFT","OPEN ENDED EVOLUTION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B3563055C60A4A0D2D68E0538909CC59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421848/2012.04751.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"bergpalmpau","last":"Berg Palm","name":"Berg Palm, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"Applications of Evolutionary Computation","status":"p","title":"Applications of Evolutionary Computation","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6e406c79-2b12-4d2d-a7ab-a2aa0aedef80"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EvoCraft: A New Challenge for Open-Endedness","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382906","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Neural Cellular Automata (NCAs) have been proven effective in simulating morphogenetic processes, the continuous construction of complex structures from very few starting cells. Recent developments in NCAs lie in the 2D domain, namely reconstructing target images from a single pixel or infinitely growing 2D textures. In this work, we propose an extension of NCAs to 3D, utilizing 3D convolutions in the proposed neural network architecture. Minecraft is selected as the environment for our automaton since it allows the generation of both static structures and moving machines. We show that despite their simplicity, NCAs are capable of growing complex entities such as castles, apartment blocks, and trees, some of which are composed of over 3,000 blocks. Additionally, when trained for regeneration, the system is able to regrow parts of simple functional machines, significantly expanding the capabilities of simulated morphogenetic systems. The code for the experiment in this paper can be found at: https://github.com/real-itu/3d-artefacts-nca.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sudhakaran, Shyam","Grbic, Djordje","Li, Siyan","Katona, Adam","Najarro, Elias","Glanois, Claire","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383561"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cellular automata","Minecraft","Neural Cellular Automata","Open ended evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"growing 000000000003d artefacts and functional machines with neural cellular automata","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421939/isal_a_00451.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383561","identifier":[{"id":"86000272077","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9cfbe7f0-0225-46d0-ac0e-eaca10caa909"],"keyword":["Minecraft","Neural Cellular Automata","cellular automata","open ended evolution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F452FA7C08B2A4307CD75B7EBE9D26C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421939/isal_a_00451.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shyam","key":"sudhakaranpau","last":"Sudhakaran","locid":"b4a6e67f-0caa-4faf-a136-bf77496f3659","name":"Sudhakaran, Shyam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Siyan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"71efb6df-0032-4f63-9a05-8489aedd9023","name":"Li, Siyan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Adam","key":"katonapau","last":"Katona","name":"Katona, Adam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["26931508"],"journal":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","volume":"2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000272077"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9cfbe7f0-0225-46d0-ac0e-eaca10caa909"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Growing 3D Artefacts and Functional Machines with Neural Cellular Automata","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383561","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
